0..74 Comment "// Two distinct keys collide under the multiply-shift family of `std.hash`"
75..135 Comment "// with an exact probability, over a uniform odd multiplier."
136..138 Comment "//"
139..214 Comment "// A universal family bounds the probability of a collision for any pair of"
215..291 Comment "// keys. So a hash table that draws its multiplier needs no assumption about"
292..361 Comment "// its keys. At `w = 8` and `m = 2` the bound is `2 / 2^m`, or `1/2`."
362..364 Comment "//"
365..443 Comment "// `multiplier 8` draws 8 bits and sets the lowest bit, so each of the 128 odd"
444..520 Comment "// multipliers has the weight `1/128`. The exact model runs each declaration"
521..595 Comment "// once for each of the 256 answers of that draw. The keys 1 and 2 collide"
596..673 Comment "// under 32 of the 128 multipliers, at `1/4`. The keys 1 and 63 collide under"
674..721 Comment "// 64 of them, at `1/2`, so the bound is tight."
722..724 Comment "//"
725..797 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/hash.gandr` — the family and the multiplier"
798..813 Comment "// - see: #5713"
815..851 Comment "// The host interface of randomness."
